{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/175750-quick-questions-about-h-tv","id":175750,"title":"Quick questions about H:tV","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-20T21:15:08-07:00","id":175750,"title":"Quick questions about H:tV","content":"Hey folks, about to run a few short Hunter games and I had a few questions I wanted to get straight.<br /> <br /> 1) When exactly does one gain the Hunter template? I'm going to be transitioning my players from straight up mortals to Hunters in my first game, so any advice on this aspect would be very helpful.<br /> <br /> 2) What are some of the side effects that come with switching over to the GMC rules via Mortal Remains? Do the specialty or extended rules changes do anything in play? I'm trying to get people's thoughts on Vigil before and after GMC.<br /> <br /> 3) Has anybody tried converting Tells over to Persistent Conditions yet? I don't expect my players to use the Code that much now that Integrity's a thing, but you never know!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T21:32:07-07:00","id":175763,"title":"","content":"Regarding 1, I wouldn't say there's a hard In-Character moment that someone stops being a mortal and becomes a Hunter. Just slap a Profession on there and start using Tactics/risking Willpower to your heart's content.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T21:33:01-07:00","id":175765,"title":"","content":"1. Risking Willpower &amp; Tactics. I guess Endowments count, too.<br /> <br /> 2. I don't think so, but for the Tactics your group might be using, you might need to look at how those extended actions are done.<br /> <br /> 3. I imagine it shouldn't be any different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T22:11:39-07:00","id":175776,"title":"","content":"1) The moment the obsession is born, the moment a character steels themselves to live this way from there on out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefo